@startuml
title UML sequence behaviour — Move focus after a keyboard delete
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam roundcorner 12
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam ArrowColor #344054
skinparam rectangle {
  BorderColor #344054
  FontColor #101828
}
skinparam package {
  BorderColor #667085
  FontColor #101828
  BackgroundColor #F9FAFB
}
actor "User" as user
box "Frontend — Angular SPA (UI components)" #E0F2FE
  participant "TodoItemComponent" as item
  participant "TodoListComponent" as list
  participant "TodoComposerComponent" as composer
  participant "TodoPageComponent" as page
end box
box "Frontend — Angular SPA (state and API client)" #E0F2FE
  participant "TodoStore" as store
end box
user -> item : Press Enter or Space on the focused delete control
item -> page : deleted output { viaKeyboard: true }
page -> store : Read visibleTodos and locate the deleted row index
store --> page : Rows and index
page -> store : delete(id)
store --> page : Row removed from visibleTodos
alt a next row exists
  page -> list : focusRequest { id: next, target: 'checkbox', seq } (L2-031)
  list --> user : Focus on the next row's checkbox
else deleted row was the last row and a previous row exists
  page -> list : focusRequest { id: previous, target: 'checkbox', seq } (L2-031)
  list --> user : Focus on the previous row's checkbox
else the list is now empty
  page -> composer : focusRequest { target: 'composer', seq } (L2-031)
  composer --> user : Focus on the composer
end
note over page, list
  Focus lands on the target row, not on the removed element,
  so the keyboard position is never lost.
  The row's checkbox receives focus. Each component applies
  focusRequest in an effect that calls focus() on a viewChild element.
end note
@enduml
